Diagnostic-only run of scripts/docker_smoke_test.sh against a scratch copy of the
repo with ONLY requirements.txt's stray first line
("Using Python 3.12.13 environment at: venv") removed. Everything else identical
to the real tree. Purpose: prove the smoke-test script itself works end-to-end
(success path) and isolate the real tree's failure to that one line.
Project: predictive-verify (separate docker compose project, cleaned up after).

Key results:
- docker compose ps: all 4 containers (api, postgres, redis, web) reported healthy
- GET /health -> {"status":"ok","model_loaded":true}
- POST /predict with X-API-Key -> 200, real churn_probability returned
- POST /predict without X-API-Key -> 401 {"error":"unauthorized",...}
- predictions table count: 0 before, 1 after (only the 200 call logged, the 401 did not)
- 61 authenticated /predict calls in <1 min -> 61st returned 429 (Redis rate limiter enforced)
- Script printed "ALL SMOKE TESTS PASSED" and exited 0

Conclusion: docker-compose.yml, Dockerfile healthchecks, Postgres logging (PRD-012),
Redis rate limiting (PRD-013), and the auth gate (PRD-054) are all genuinely wired
correctly. The ONLY defect preventing this from working on the real, current tree
is the stray first line of requirements.txt. This does NOT change the real-tree
verdict for PRD-029 / PRD-046a, which remain FAIL/blocked on the actual repo state.
